## Biographies
Xiaoqun Dong received her B.S. degree in 2015 from Yulin Normal University, China. Now she is a Master candidate of analytical chemistry at Sichuan University. Her research interests include synthesis of nanomaterials and their application in chemical sensor.
Yingying Su received her PhD from Sichuan University in 2007. Now she works at Analytical & Testing Center, Sichuan University, China. Her areas of interest are separation technique, chemiluminescence and luminescence-based sensor.
Ting Lu received her M.S. in analytical chemistry from the College of Chemistry at Sichuan University in 2017 under the supervision of Prof. Yi Lv. Now she works at Tianjin High School, China.
Lichun Zhang received her PhD in analytical chemistry from the College of Chemistry at Sichuan University in 2010. Now she is an associate professor in the College of  Chemistry, Sichuan University. Her scientific interests focus on chemical sensor based on cataluminescence.
Lianqian Wu received her B.S. degree in 2015 from Sichuan University, China. Now she is a Master candidate of analytical chemistry at Sichuan University. Her research interests are focused on synthesis of nanocomposites and their application in chemical sensor.
Yi Lv is a full professor in College of Chemistry and director of Analytical & Testing  Center at Sichuan University, China. He obtained his PhD degree in 2005 from Southwest China Normal University (currently Southwest University), China. After a  two-year stay at Tsinghua University as a postdoctoral researcher, he joined the faculty of Sichuan University in 2005. His research interests are mainly in the areas of analytical spectrometry and nano-materials for sensors. He is the author or coauthor of ${\sim}120$ journal papers and one book chapter.
